# Regenerable experiment output. The per-point CSVs run to hundreds of megabytes; the metrics
# they reduce to (code/out/*.json, metrics_*.csv, runs_*.csv) ARE tracked, so the tables, the
# figures and audit_numbers.py all run without repeating the runs.
code/out/baselines/
code/out/sample/
code/out/solve/
code/out/stale_*/
code/out/log_*.txt

# Build artifacts
code/bin/
code/probe/bin/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/

# Figures are tracked as PDF; the PNG copies exist only for quick viewing
code/figs/*.png

# Not redistributable: the NIMS MatNavi terms of use forbid passing their tables to third
# parties, so every file that carries the steel records is excluded. See DATA.md; prep_data.py
# rebuilds them from your own MatNavi download. The trained surrogate (models/steel.json plus
# .bin) is a derived model and is kept, as are the split roles and the column ranges.
code/data/steel.csv
code/nd/steel/
code/models/steel_predictions.csv
code/models/steel_nd_predictions.csv
code/models/opennn_trained/steel_predictions.csv

# The paper itself is NOT part of this reproducibility-only repo (code, data and figures only).
paper/

# Internal working docs (not part of the public reproducibility repo)
AUDIT_DECISIONS.md
PLAN.md
notes/
email_propuesta_titulo.txt

# Python
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
